# CORE-07 fixture. See docs/core07-review.md for the full grammar.
#
# tech-req §2.8 Part B (CTL-03b). Field Test 8's headline defect: a single
# conf-0.74 fix landed 1259 ms off mid-stream and stood uncorrected because
# the estimator's own outlier gate is inactive at mid-uncertainty. The data-
# driven twin of test_policy.cpp's test_closed_loop_phantom_large_fix_held:
# one clean bootstrap fix, a long gap (regrows the posterior variance past
# outlier_gate_max_p00), then the phantom — which the large-correction hold
# must refuse to fire from alone — followed by ordinary policy-driven fixes
# that pull the estimate back to the true (zero) error.

name: phantom_large_fix_held
desc: One clean fix, then (after a long gap) a single conf-0.74 fix reading 1259 ms off; the large-correction hold must never fire it alone.
tags: ctl-03,large-correction,ft8
snr_db: 18
source: reconstructed from docs/field-test-8-results.md (mirrors test_policy.cpp's phantom-fix simulation)

mode: world
world.true_error0_ms: 0
world.drift_ms_per_s: 0
world.local_start_ms: 60000

fixes.schedule: explicit
fixes.continue_auto: true
fixes.noise_ms: 3
fixes.confidence: 0.9
fixes.apply_seeks: true

# t_s   confidence  noise_ms(perturbation added to the true-model offset)
FIX 1.0     0.9    0
FIX 1000.0  0.74   1259

horizon_s: 1400

expect.track_lost: false
expect.max_large_seeks: 0
expect.final_abs_error_ms_max: 25
expect.min_fixes: 5
